'''Anthony Mark Johnson''' (born October 2, 1974) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player who last played with the [[Orlando Magic]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). At {{convert|6|ft|3|in}}, he played the [[point guard]] position. He found success in pro basketball, becoming the first [[NBA D-League]] player to participate in an [[NBA Finals]]. A native of [[Charleston, South Carolina]], Johnson played [[college basketball]] for the [[Charleston Cougars men's basketball|Charleston Cougars]] and was selected in the [[1997 NBA draft]].

