'''Anthony Jarrad Morrow''' (born September 27, 1985) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player and executive who was most recently an executive for the [[Oklahoma City Thunder]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA).<ref>{{Cite web|title=Nick Collison To Take On New Role In Thunder Front Office|url=https://www.nba.com/thunder/news/release-collison-210810|url-status=live|access-date=November 9, 2021|website=Oklahoma City Thunder|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210810163103/https://www.nba.com/thunder/news/release-collison-210810 |archive-date=August 10, 2021 }}</ref> He played [[college basketball]] for [[Georgia Tech Yellow Jackets men's basketball|Georgia Tech]]. He went undrafted in the [[2008 NBA draft]] but was later signed by the [[Golden State Warriors]]. He was best known for his three-point shooting.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.welcometoloudcity.com/2014/7/12/5893785/anthony-morrow-three-point-shooter-oklahoma-city-thunder-free-agency|title=What the Morrow signing means for the Thunder|work=Welcome to Loud City|access-date=2018-09-15}}</ref>

