'''Anthony Harris Bennett''' (born March 14, 1993) is a Canadian professional [[basketball]] player for [[Al-Najma SC (Bahrain)|Al-Najma]] of the [[Bahraini Premier League (basketball)|Bahraini Premier League]]. He played [[college basketball]] for the [[University of Nevada, Las Vegas]] (UNLV) for one year. He was the [[List of first overall NBA draft picks|first overall pick]] in the [[2013 NBA draft]] by the [[Cleveland Cavaliers]], becoming the first Canadian to be drafted number one overall.<ref name="Huffington Post">{{cite news|first=Chris|last=Greenberg|url=http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2013/06/27/anthony-bennett-pick-cavaliers-cleveland_n_3513282.html|title=Anthony Bennett Goes No. 1 In 2013 NBA Draft To Cleveland Cavaliers|work=HuffingtonPost.com|date=June 27, 2013|access-date=June 30, 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230414193504/https://www.huffpost.com/entry/anthony-bennett-pick-cavaliers-cleveland_n_3513282 |archive-date=14 April 2023}}</ref> He played only four seasons in the NBA, averaging 4.4 points per game, and has been named the worst number-one pick in league history.<ref>
